    # 2026-09-08 — BISECTED IN THE VERDICT STORE, AND THERE IS NOTHING AT HEAD TO
    # BISECT. Median over a FIXED set of 6166 test names present in all 26 full
    # runs from 09-05 05:41 to 09-08 07:07 (a fixed set, so a suite that changes
    # size cannot explain a move): flat at 2.24-2.29 s, 22 of 26 within +/-1.5%,
    # and HEAD today (2.2387) is BELOW the recorded range's start (2.2825).
    # Two excursions, each back on the shelf at the next reading: 830/831
    # (96fdf6235) 2.585 = +13.7%, and 876 (ffe9a2cbb) 4.102 = +81%.
    # ⚠ NOT ATTRIBUTED, AND THIS COLUMN CANNOT ATTRIBUTE IT. These are wall-clock
    # seconds under `ctest -j32` on a shared box, i.e. two SEPARATELY measured
    # columns; the same instrument shows +81% one row away. A code cause is not
    # excluded either — a9c7b67fd..96fdf6235 does carry 305/171 lines of real
    # compiler source over ten files. 876 vs 877 share a head AND a build
    # timestamp but differ in lib_hash, so they are probably armed vs unarmed
    # and are NOT a clean same-binary control; I do not lean on them.
    # The measurement that would settle it is not a bisect: compile a fixed
    # program set with both binaries INTERLEAVED IN ONE PROCESS. Until someone
    # names a commit worth that, the honest state is: not present at HEAD.
