vg_leak_records            sweep     87  sandbox/vg-round2/{leaks.tsv,recs2.pkl}
    # 2026-09-08 RE-MEASURED on build 8e5f92705b285d29 43 with the per-fixture CMake
    # flags the first sweep dropped. 87 of the 90 still leak (old-closure-explicit-types,
    # issue-19367-b170 and rfc2229_move_disjoint_field are now CLEAN — fixed since the
    # vgfix build, which no longer exists). THE GROUPING THE ENTRY ASKED FOR, over 270
    # loss records / 90 fixtures, 202 of them stdlib-allocated:
    #     39  distinct IMMEDIATE allocation sites   <- the coarsest honest row unit
    #     75  distinct (site, caller) pairs
    #    110  distinct full allocation stacks
    # So 90 hits is AT MOST 39 rows, not 90. The largest class is `vec$vec_new` reached
    # from the fixture's own `mk` — 141 records over 32 fixtures — and ONE root inside it
    # is now proven and rowed (soundness_queue `replace_site_skips_field_drop_glue`): the
    # field drop glue is emitted only for a top-level local at scope exit, never at an
    # assignment/replace site nor through a struct field. HOW MANY OF THE 32 THAT ROOT
    # ACCOUNTS FOR IS NOT MEASURED and must not be claimed. ⚠ Two negative controls that
    # cost this round real time: a plain `struct{Vec} + impl Drop` local does NOT leak,
    # and a `Vec<T>` ELEMENT with a user Drop does NOT leak — so neither "user drop
    # replaces glue" nor "container element glue" is the shape. What remains unattributed:
    # 28 records allocated in `main`, 14 in `String__grow`, 8 in `buf_reader_wrap`, and
    # ~15 one-fixture sites in writ/fabric/zvec arenas that may well be deliberate.

run_oracle_c90_population_hole  defect  20  scripts/run_oracle.py, measured 2026-09-08c
    # THE RUNTIME ORACLE'S RUN POPULATION IS 6533, NOT 6553, AND ITS SILENCE ABOUT THE
    # OTHER 20 HAS BEEN READ AS COVERAGE. `run_oracle.py:65` sets ccrc=90 ("exited 0
    # after self-diagnosing", the 14th bug kind) when logosc exits 0 AND stderr matches
    # `^(mlir_gen|sema|mono): ` — and then `if cc != 0: return` NEVER LINKS AND NEVER
    # RUNS the program. The regex does not exclude `warning:`. Re-run by hand on all 20
    # sources (WITHOUT run_oracle's per-fixture flags and env): 16 of them match only on
    # a `warning:` line (e.g. hrtb-double-quantifier prints "mlir_gen: warning: no MLIR
    # type for TypeVar 'X'") and compile rc 0 — instrument false positives, and 16
    # programs the runtime column has never executed.
    # ⚠ THE OTHER 4 ARE NOT EXPLAINED AND ARE THE MEASUREMENT THIS ENTRY OWES:
    #   imported/pass/match/issue-41888-b170            mlir_gen: internal: unknown tagged enum 'Result__void__<error>'
    #   imported/pass/match/nested-tuple-in-variant-payload-b170  same, 'Result__(i64, (i64, i64))__<error>'
    #   imported/pass/option-result/res-and-or-comb-or  same, 'Result__i32__F'
    #   spec/pass/intrinsic_2                           mlir_gen: internal: unsupported cast: no lowering from 'i32' to metaprog Type array
    # BY HAND ALL FOUR EXIT rc 1 — an honest refusal, NOT the 14th kind. But ccrc=90 is
    # only reachable when rc IS 0, so under run_oracle's own invocation (cwd=build,
    # per-fixture `extra` flags and env from the cmake registry) they exited 0 WITH that
    # line. THE MEASUREMENT: reproduce all four under run_oracle's exact argv/env/cwd and
    # say whether the exit code really differs. If it does, the 14th kind — recorded
    # CLOSED 2026-08-22 by `0f4083f7` — has four live instances and each is a tier-1 row.
    # If it does not, the entry is 20 instrument false positives and closes at zero.
    # ⚠ TOOLING IS FROZEN: this entry records the hole, it does not authorise fixing the
    # regex. Do not "fix" run_oracle to make the number go away.

